# Real client invoices — NEVER commit. See README.md § DPDP handling.
# These are real client financial documents under the DPDP Act, not the
# fictitious spike data P0-06's runs/ captured. The whole reason ADR 0008
# self-hosts OCR is to keep this class of document off third-party
# infrastructure; committing it to a git remote would defeat that at the
# first step. The rule is kept here, in the spike directory, so it travels
# with the data rather than depending on a file three levels up — the same
# reasoning as P0-07's .gitignore, and the gap that caused P0-06 finding #13.
real-samples/
real-results/

# The spike's own virtualenv. PaddlePaddle + PaddleX pull ~2GB of wheels;
# this is regenerable from requirements.txt and must never be committed.
.venv/

# Downloaded PP-StructureV3 model weights (~1GB), fetched on first run.
models/
.paddlex/

__pycache__/
